  "notes": "Two things this pins. (a) The one clamp (M-26): watched_ms <= content_duration_ms x (loop_count + 1) whenever the duration is known, with loop_count capped at 20, applied to every running total the session takes under GREATEST, heartbeats included, not only the play_end figure. Rewatched seconds within a session are genuine watch time but they are bounded the same way looping is, so twenty-five passes of a 5 s flick are credited as the twenty-one the capped loop_count can account for: 105000, with watched_ms_reported keeping the client's 130000 for audit. Before M-26 the clamp bound only play_end and the heartbeats' 130000 survived through GREATEST. (b) Android divergence 2 (M-12), closed 12 Sep 2026: VideoWatchTracker.accumulateWatched used to increment loopCount on a wrap and then still apply the forward-jump ceiling to the wrap delta, so a wrap whose tail + head exceeded two ticks was counted as a loop AND its watch time discarded as a seek. Both trackers now credit a wrap in full and skip the ceiling for it."
